## Common Gotchas

- Never pass explicit ``tenant_id`` to CRUD/service calls — the
  TenantAwareCRUD seam injects the request context's tenant and blocks
  caller-supplied overrides (logged as ``tenant_id_override_blocked``)
- Service methods take ``current_user`` (the authenticated principal), not
  bare ``user_id``/``tenant_id`` kwargs
- Service methods should validate ownership before updates/deletes
- Use ``model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`` for partial updates
- Response schemas use ``ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)``
- Raise domain errors (``ModelNotFoundError``, ``DuplicateError``,
  ``ForbiddenError``) — never HTTP-shaped exceptions from the service layer

## Registration Checklist (post-generation)

After generating this module, complete these registration steps:

1. Add the model import to `src/app/models/__init__.py` (single registration point)
2. Register the router in `src/app/api/v1/__init__.py`
3. Generate a migration with RLS: `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m 'Add {{ table_name }} table'`
   — then add `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`, `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`, and
   the `tenant_isolation` + `bypass_rls` policies to the new table (see
   `src/migrations/versions/08_enable_rls_policies.py` for the pattern);
   `CREATE TABLES_ON_STARTUP`-created tables silently lack RLS policies
